===============================================================================
1. Clean-Room Windows Implementation & Zero Third-Party Dependencies
===============================================================================

This project is a clean-room implementation developed entirely in Windows
PowerShell (compatible with Windows PowerShell 5.1 and PowerShell 7+) and
native Win32 / .NET APIs.

- Zero Bundled Third-Party Code: This repository bundles no third-party
  libraries, binary executables, node modules, or external PowerShell modules.
- Zero Runtime Dependencies: All filesystem handle-bound deletion routines,
  registry queries, Win32 P/Invoke structures, cryptographic hashing, and
  serialization logic utilize standard built-in Windows platform interfaces.

===============================================================================
2. Conceptual Origin & Architectural Independence
===============================================================================

The conceptual idea of auditing and cleaning local Claude-related artifacts
was inspired by the macOS-oriented shell script project:
- suyuan2022/claude-cleanup (https://github.com/suyuan2022/suyuan-skill)

Architectural Separation & Non-Ported Features:
- No code was copied or ported from the upstream macOS project.
- Backup, trash/recycle-bin, and device-identity rotation or anti-abuse
  modification behaviors present in upstream scripts were intentionally NOT
  ported or implemented.
- The Windows Claude Cleanup Toolkit was independently designed from scratch to
  address Windows-specific architectures, including NTFS reparse point
  protection, Windows Security Identifiers (SID) ownership verification,
  Win32 handle-bound file disposition, atomic execution ledger persistence,
  Windows Registry key validation, and Windows Package Management (MSIX/AppX).

